      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Assuming the contribution from gametic phase disequilibrium to be negligible, Mode and Robinson (1959) showed how the genetic covariance can be subdivided into various components. Their work is a straightforward extension of the results of Cockerham (1954) and Kempthorne (1954) for single characters. In order to simplify the presentation, recall the procedure used in Chapter 5 for decomposing the total genotypic value of a trait influenced by two loci. For characters 1 and 2, we have",
